  "date": "2026-09-26",
  "subject": "Fail-before-construction cache-only execution on Windows and Debian",
  "claim": "The current compiler, split-project WVB and segmented hosted application builders enforce prepared-product mode. Exact hits validate and materialize; misses return 64 before native construction; corrupt entries fail closed. Both hosts pass the focused lifecycle owners and a real binder miss/prepare/hit/later-miss/hit sequence, preserving existing outputs and completed caches. The packaged binder executes its expected usage rejection on both hosts. CI phase integration remains unfinished.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "Other",
    "value": "6038ecdc plus the exact changed implementation and verifier identities recorded in runs. Cache tests use bounded fixture producers; the separate measured binder sequence uses retained native tools and a 774724-byte previously compiled binder WVB."
  },
