  "limitations": [
    "This adds an enforceable construction boundary, not a completed CI workflow. It neither refreshes the entire current compiler nor claims complete affected-owner execution or qualification. The mode only applies to the three named builders.",
    "The 816-byte legacy and 221-byte minimum-program probes failed existing packaging: the enum metadata reader rejects zero nominal types. A 1281-byte nominal fixture failed staging with Unsupported_module detail=105. Those failed probes were diagnosed and retained locally; their failures were not relabeled as passes. The first Windows long-path probe additionally reported transport status 70; path sensitivity is an inference, not an isolated measurement.",
    "The successful measurement uses the binder WVB already packaged in prior evidence. Each host starts a fresh private cache, uses one five-minute deadline for the complete sequence, and validates exact output bytes on every reuse or rejected profile change. Windows and Debian ran concurrently; this is one construction/reuse observation, not a throughput regression threshold. Peak working set was not measured.",
    "Windows used Node 24.18.0; Debian WSL used Node 20.19.2 and the repository on /mnt/d. Debian has no pwsh installation, so its existing Node leaf owners were invoked directly. The first split-cache run exposed a test expectation using prepared mode for an existing ordinary-construction producer-identity case; the test restored that case to ordinary mode before the passing rerun.",
    "Routing verification passed 31 general and 304 native cases. Broad compiler/runtime conformance, independent reconstruction, database behavior and release qualification were not run: the changed contract is cache-only acquisition and rejection, not compilation semantics.",
    "CI run 36275830472 timed out on Windows and failed the Linux ordinary console-packager source reconstructed-WVB-size assertion. The packager projects were migrated to Project 4 after that older byte-pinned verifier was written. This needs reconciliation and is not treated as passing CI evidence."
